              "line": 1,
              "text": "ETC (electron transport chain) carriers are located on the inner mitochondrial membrane. ETC is the final pathway by which all the electrons derived from oxidation of carbohydrates, fatty acids, and amino acids are directed towards the final reaction with oxygen to form water and ATP.",
